{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8033","id":5222605614,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABN0qjLg","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8033","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8033.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8033.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8033","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8033/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8033/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8033/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/5d63b51790cc9b710fad0e453654702468793797","number":8033,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(fleet): probe-based UDS/TCP transport selection for broker clients (#6218)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements #6218 (from the #5699 design adopted 2026-11-05): fleet clients select UDS vs TCP per broker role by probing, instead of fixed routes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **fleet-config**: new `RoleTransport` + `Config::role_transport_choice(role)` + `probe_socket(path)`. Selection order: the `[<role>] transport` config preference wins (\"tcp\" = TCP without probing, \"socket\" = the role's Unix socket); with no preference, probe the role socket — file exists + connect succeeds selects UDS, absent or stale selects TCP. Probe behavior is unit-tested for socket-present, socket-absent, and socket-stale cases, plus the pure preference/probe matrix.\n- **queue client** (`fleet-queue`, client feature now depends on fleet-config):\n  - `broker_sock()` asks fleet-config instead of hardcoding `~/.cache/laptop-agent/broker.sock` (env > config file > the same compiled-in default; load error falls back to the home-anchored path).\n  - Direct path is route-selected: an explicit `REPO_QUEUE_BROKER_URL` / broker-url file wins and gains a `unix://<path>` form; otherwise the probe choice for the queue-broker role selects a direct UDS roundtrip when the socket answers. A failed UDS attempt falls back to the session-proxy (TCP) route within the same call. Sandbox consumers are untouched: with no live role socket the client keeps the session-proxy route exactly as before.\n- **queue-broker `DirectSecrets`**: gains a `unix://` form for `QUEUE_BROKER_SECRETS_URL` (same GET /secret/<name> exchange over the secrets broker's socket; connect failure falls back to the TCP endpoint in the same resolve), and the default endpoint is probe-selected via fleet-config when no URL is configured. Response handling is shared between the legs.\n- **`fleet secrets` (laptop-local path)**: new `DirectBrokerSource` in fleet-secrets speaks plain HTTP over the secrets broker's own socket, reading the broker token from its token file. `Resolver::default_chain` prepends it only when the probe selects the socket (laptop); on the sandbox the chain is byte-for-byte the historical shape. `fleet secrets list` uses the direct source on the same condition.\n\n## Tests\n\nLaptop, `pkgs/fleet`:\n- `cargo test -p fleet-config` — 26 passed (3 new: preference/probe matrix, probe live/absent/stale, role dispatch)\n- `cargo test -p fleet-queue --all-features` — 119 passed (new: configured-URL routing, shared response parsing, DirectSecrets endpoint selection + status mapping, UDS resolve roundtrip)\n- `cargo test -p fleet-secrets` — all passed (new: direct source resolve + list roundtrips over a temp socket, 404 mapping)\n- `cargo test -p fleet -p fleet-dispatch` — all suites ok\n\nQueue task 14372 (lane code-h, direct execution lane).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796813083&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8033&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8033&signature=e84df8724ce8d15660b80535fcb72c21196f43bb723229cec695fa99a1f6dfd5\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8033?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T10:44:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T11:08:10Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T11:08:08Z","